    "text": "Four ground-truth/parsed formula pairs separated by a blue line, all symbols boxed green: 7^2 vs 72, 10^{-1} vs 10 − 1, x_{(i−1)} vs x(i − 1), and blackboard ℕ ⊂ ℝ vs italic N ⊂ R. These are the examples of CDM giving matches despite positional or symbol differences.",
